# Selecting Data

In Lesson 7, students discover that a model can fit its training data perfectly and still make terrible predictions, if that data doesn't match the real world it's being used in.

Anita's ice cream shop wants to predict monthly sales. She finds a model online and uses it.

## Anita's Ice Cream Shop Sales Predictions

<div style="text-align: center; margin: 20px auto;">
  <img src="https://images.code.org/ba99fbbc4f2797e5462a0419217fc19e-image-1794514220142.png" alt="A chart showing predicted ice cream sales declining from about 400 units in January to about 100 units in July" style="width: 55%; border-radius: 10px;">
</div>

The model predicts Anita will sell around 400 units in January and only around 100 in July, the opposite of what a US ice cream shop should expect. The model fits its training data well. The problem is where that data came from: an ice cream shop in Australia, where the seasons are flipped, it's hotter in January than July.


## Lesson Vocabulary

<div style="background-color: #F7F7FB; border-left: 4px solid #4C42CF; border-radius: 8px; padding: 12px 16px; margin: 16px 0;">
  <div style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.5;"><strong>&#128214; Biased data:</strong> data that doesn't accurately represent the real-world situations in which a model will be used.</div>
</div>

<div style="background-color: #F7F7FB; border-left: 4px solid #4C42CF; border-radius: 8px; padding: 12px 16px; margin: 16px 0;">
  <div style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.5;"><strong>&#128214; Representative data:</strong> data that accurately represents the real-world situations in which a model will be used.</div>
</div>

<div style="background-color: #E4E2F8; border-radius: 10px; padding: 16px 20px; margin: 16px 0;">
  <div style="font-size: 16px; color: #222222; line-height: 1.5;"><strong>&#128161; Teacher tip:</strong> this is the core idea worth repeating: a model is only as good as the data it's trained on. Good model fit doesn't mean good predictions, if the training context doesn't match the real-world context, the model will confidently get it wrong.</div>
</div>


